```java
// Tracking unique visitor IDs in a List - bug-prone and slow
List<String> visitors = new ArrayList<>();
if (!visitors.contains(id)) {   // O(n) scan on every check
    visitors.add(id);
}
// Duplicates still possible under races; contains() is linear.
```
Using `contains` on a `List` to enforce uniqueness scans every element each time, so the work grows with the list.

```java
import java.util.*;

// Unique IDs, fast membership -> Set
Set<String> visitors = new HashSet<>();
visitors.add(id);               // O(1), duplicates auto-rejected

// Need insertion order kept -> LinkedHashSet
Set<String> ordered = new LinkedHashSet<>();

// Need sorted iteration -> TreeSet
Set<String> sorted = new TreeSet<>();

// Key to value lookup -> Map
Map<String, Integer> counts = new HashMap<>();
counts.merge(id, 1, Integer::sum);  // count occurrences in O(1)
```
The `HashSet` rejects duplicates for free in O(1); the right structure removes the bug instead of patching it.

